# L §4.6 step 4 Ties (tally 2.1.7 R4, issue #143): two pins of one set on one cell, keys written alike with no
# variable, tie where load sees them: LOAD-OVERLAP. The literal twin of L4_6_cascade_pins' run-time tie. 2.1.6's
# refcore let the later pin win (8).
=== m.tally
model c7b
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"

index ks = [k1, k2]

input r[k in ks]: num

def tot: num = sum(r[k] for k in ks) at reader

ask e: tot as if {r[k1] = 5, r[k1] = 7} law 2026-06-30

version v
  cite card
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r[*] = 1 "c"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-OVERLAP pins r[k1] = 5 and r[k1] = 7 of r overlap at [k1] ...
